  "description": "WEGLIG crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C60 H96 Gd8 Ge12 N4 O64,2(C12 H8 N2),16(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.824-3.841 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 109.67-110.92°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C84H144Gd8Ge12N8O80. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 24 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 16 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
